# config/local-apps — local tools to expose in the desktop launcher (Vicinae).
#
# Vicinae is a desktop-entry launcher: it reads .desktop files, not $PATH. Tools
# that live only in ~/.local/bin are therefore invisible to it unless we generate
# .desktop entries for them. This file is that source of truth.
#
# One tool per line:
#   <basename> [Display Name]
#   - basename  : looked up in ~/.local/bin
#   - Display Name : optional; defaults to the basename (any number of words)
#
# Regenerate (writes managed files to ~/.local/share/applications/):
#   scripts/generate-local-apps.sh
# Remove all managed entries:
#   scripts/generate-local-apps.sh --remove
#
# All generated entries default to Terminal=true (these are CLI/TUI tools). If one
# is actually a GUI, edit its generated .desktop and set Terminal=false.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed: pip/pip3/pip3.12, the odf*/xml2odf/mailodf/csv2ods
# LibreOffice CLI tools, pymupdf, slack-mcp, mise. Those are utilities you call
# with arguments, not apps you launch. Add any of them here if you want them
# reachable from the launcher.

TUICommander.AppImage   TUI Commander
tuios
slk
vi-sql
